## v4 — Staff roles, commission, payouts, W2 withholding, Stripe Connect, statements
================================================================================
Turns the multi-stylist app into a real salon-with-employees model.

### Roles (owner vs stylist) — a stylist must NOT see what the owner sees
- Owner (`stylists.is_owner=true`): full admin — all tabs incl. Analytics (business-wide),
  Staff, Settings, and a **Payouts** manager across all stylists.
- Stylist (`is_owner=false`): a RESTRICTED dashboard — only their own Calendar, Appointments
  (pending/confirm), Clients, Services, Schedule, Messages, and a new **Earnings** tab. They do
  NOT see Analytics, Staff, Settings, or any other stylist's data. Enforced by (a) the tab set in
  AdminDashboard keyed off `isOwner`, and (b) RLS/`stylist_id` scoping already on every table.

### Commission + W2 withholding (owner-controlled; stylist can't edit their own)
- `stylists.commission_rate numeric` (default **0.55** = 55%), editable per stylist by the owner in
  the Staff manager. `stylists.is_w2 bool` + `tax_withholding_rate numeric` (owner-set).
- Payout math per completed appointment: `gross = service_total_cents` (revenue),
  `commission = round(gross * commission_rate)`, `withholding = is_w2 ? round(commission * tax_withholding_rate) : 0`,
  `net = commission - withholding`. Sum over a period for a statement. Money in integer cents.
- **Security:** commission_rate/is_w2/tax_withholding_rate/stripe_account_id/payouts_enabled are
  guarded by the `guard_stylist_owner_flag` trigger — only the owner (via service-role admin API) or
  migrations can write them; the stylist's browser session cannot.

### Earnings + statements (stylist-facing)
- Stylist **Earnings** tab: their completed services (line items), the commission calc
  (gross → commission % → withholding → net), period totals, and downloadable **statements** (CSV,
  reuse the finance-CSV pattern with formula-injection neutralization + pagination).

### Bank linking + payouts — **Stripe Connect (Express), test mode**
- Stylist links their OWN bank via Stripe's hosted onboarding (Claude never sees/enters bank
  details). `POST /api/admin/connect` → find-or-create Express account (`stylists.stripe_account_id`)
  + return an Account Link URL; the stylist completes KYC + bank on Stripe. Webhook `account.updated`
  → set `payouts_enabled`. Earnings tab shows "Link bank" or "Bank linked ✓".
- Owner **Payouts** manager: per stylist + period, shows computed net; "Send payout" → `stripe.transfers.create`
  to the connected account (test mode), writes a `payouts` row (status paid, stripe_transfer_id).
  Also a "Mark paid manually" fallback (method='manual') for cash/Zelle. Gracefully degrade if
  Connect isn't enabled on the platform test account (show a clear message; manual payout still works).
- `payouts` ledger table (period, gross/commission/withholding/net, status, method, transfer id) with
  RLS `stylist_id = current_stylist_id()` so a stylist reads only their own statements.

### New-stylist bookability (fixed)
- Adding a stylist clones the owner's catalog (`clone_catalog(from,to)` SECURITY DEFINER) so they are
  immediately bookable; `/api/stylists` still filters to stylists with ≥1 active service.

