## v5 — Stylist lockdown, geofenced time clock, first-login password, avatars, earnings detail
================================================================================

### Role lockdown (a stylist sees almost nothing of the business)
- Non-owner dashboard tabs = ONLY **calendar** + **earnings**. No appointments/clients/services/
  schedule/messages/analytics/staff/settings/payouts. The **Deposits collected** stat is owner-only.
- The stylist **calendar** is money-free: appointment blocks show client name + time + service only —
  NO deposit/balance/price, no charge-balance, no fee panel. Owner view unchanged. Driven by an
  `isOwner` prop on AdminCalendar from AdminDashboard. Server APIs already scope by `stylist_id`.

### Geofenced time clock
- `time_entries` (clock_in/out + lat/lng + source geo|admin). Business location on the OWNER row
  (`workplace_lat/lng`, `workplace_radius_m` default 150m), set in Settings ("use my current
  location"). Clock in/out allowed ONLY within radius (haversine), validated on client AND server
  (`/api/admin/timeclock` → 403 not_at_workplace / 400 if unset). `ClockWidget` sits atop the
  calendar tab. Owner **Timesheets** tab edits any entry (source='admin').

### First-login password change
- New staff are created with `must_change_password=true` (temp password). `admin/page.tsx` renders a
  ChangePassword gate before the dashboard when the flag is set; on change → `auth.updateUser` +
  `/api/admin/change-password` clears the flag (service-role; the guard trigger blocks the browser
  from clearing it to skip the gate). The seeded demo stylist (Bianca) is exempt.

### Staff avatars + earnings detail
- Owner uploads each stylist's **profile picture** in the Staff manager (reuses /api/admin/upload →
  `stylists.avatar_url`).
- Earnings line = **style + variant** ("Box Braids Large — Midback length"), amount charged, the
  literal calc ("$200 × 55%"), the payout ($110), plus **this-week** and **this-month** totals
  (America/Chicago). computeEarnings joins service_variants for the label; cents math unchanged.

### Suspend / disable a stylist (owner)
- `stylists.is_active` (default true). Owner toggles Suspend/Enable per stylist in the Staff manager.
  Suspended stylists are excluded from `/api/stylists` (booking picker), rejected at `/api/bookings/hold`
  (409), and shown an "Account suspended" screen instead of the admin dashboard. Owner can't suspend self.

### Phone required at booking
- The booking wizard requires a valid phone (≥10 digits) before checkout, and `/api/bookings/hold`
  enforces it server-side (`clientPhone` ≥10 digits) — 400 otherwise.

### Workplace geofence coords
- Set the workplace by the owner clicking "Use my current location" in Settings (captures exact GPS, so
  clock-in distance ≈ 0 and cancels GPS bias). A geocoded street address can sit 100–250m off the actual
  standing spot; prefer the button. Radius is adjustable (default 150m).

### Stylist calendar is VIEW-ONLY + contact-free (hardened)
- A stylist's calendar shows client NAME + time + service only. Gated on `canSeeMoney` (=isOwner):
  no lifecycle actions (confirm/decline/complete/no_show/cancel/revert), no reschedule, no drag-to-
  reschedule, no "New appointment", no money, and NO client email/phone. Enforced in the UI AND at the
  data layer — `/api/admin/appointments` zeroes money and nulls client email/phone/CRM for non-owners
  (they get name-only). Owner (isOwner) view is unchanged/full.

### Deposit is one configurable number, reflected everywhere
- Owner sets it in Settings → it writes `cancellation_policy.deposit_cents` and propagates to every
  service's `deposit_flat_cents`. Client-facing copy (services page, services grid, policies page) and
  the booking pricing all derive the amount dynamically — no hardcoded "$50". The e2e suites read the
  live deposit from the catalog so a deposit change never breaks the money assertions.

### Guard trigger now protects (server-only writes)
is_owner, commission_rate, is_w2, tax_withholding_rate, stripe_account_id, payouts_enabled,
must_change_password, workplace_lat/lng/radius_m, is_active — a stylist's browser session can change none.

